---
config:
  flowchart:
    nodeSpacing: 24
---
flowchart TB
    accTitle: How the German documentation stays in step
    accDescr: README.md and README.de.md link to each other. The English pages of the website, such as guide.md, take their snippets from README.md, and the German ones, such as guide.de.md, from README.de.md; an English page shows the diagram NAME.mmd, its German twin NAME.de.mmd. scripts/check-project.sh compares the outline of each German page with that of its English twin. MkDocs builds the English website and, with the plugin i18n, the German one in de/, with a language switch in the header. The English sources are blue, the German ones orange, the check and the website green.

    readme["README.md"]
    readmede["README.de.md"]
    guide["`docs/guide.md<br>*and the other pages*`"]
    guidede["`docs/guide.de.md<br>*and the other German pages*`"]
    diagram["docs/diagrams/NAME.mmd"]
    diagramde["docs/diagrams/NAME.de.mmd"]
    check{"`scripts/check-project.sh<br>*the same headings, snippets<br>and diagrams, in order?*`"}
    site(["`Website<br>*English in /, German in de/,<br>a language switch in the header*`"])

    readme <-- "language switch" --> readmede
    readme -- "snippets" --> guide
    readmede -- "snippets" --> guidede
    diagram --> guide
    diagramde --> guidede
    guide --> check
    guidede --> check
    check -- "yes" --> site

    classDef english fill:#526cfe2e,stroke:#526cfe,stroke-width:2px
    classDef german fill:#f59e0b2e,stroke:#f59e0b,stroke-width:2px
    classDef done fill:#16a34a2e,stroke:#16a34a,stroke-width:2px
    class readme,guide,diagram english
    class readmede,guidede,diagramde german
    class check,site done
